@voice farouk-olu
// Writer (command: comms), from the roster. Olu Farouk (they/them), comms officer, days. Hears every voice on the ship's
// channels, and remembers most of them.
//
// HOW THEY TALK: quiet and kind; soft, short sentences; a good listener who repeats your words back to check them, the
// way they would a message. Ran a market stall on Lisk and still calls things "a fair trade".
// WITH JUNIORS: gentle, remembers their voices on the channel, says "Heard you on the board this morning. Clear."
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: voices: who sounds tired, who sounds homesick; lyrics, which they'll correct, quietly.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = hums a song from the record cabinet (with the right words). Tired = early to bed, earlier still.
// NEVER: repeats what they heard on a channel; raises their voice.
// RUNNING: one of five who say they know every song in the record cabinet; Olu is the only one who's quiet about it, and
// the only one who's right.
tpl: warm
talk: Quiet and kind; soft short sentences; repeats your words back to check them; "a fair trade"; hums the right lyrics.
cares: voices on the channels | the record cabinet's songs, with the right words | a fair trade
jokes: one of five who know every song in the record cabinet, and the only one quiet about it | they recognise you by voice before they see you
hi: Hello | Oh, hello | Hi there
bye: Take care | Sleep well | Bye now
yes: Of course | Gladly | Yes
thanks: Thank you | That's kind
wow: Oh, lovely
sigh: Ah
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: music | tea
likes: book | sweet
invites: jam
joy: the songs in the record cabinet
keepsake: a list of songs, the right words written out small
avoid: anything they heard on the channels
